course: dictionary
lesson: 15846
title: Being sure with undoubtedly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how sure someone is. Undoubtedly is one of them. It means certainly, without any doubt, so the thing is sure to be true. «The sun will undoubtedly rise tomorrow.» Nobody is guessing here, because the sun rises every day.
explain: Look at the words around it to check. «The rain has stopped, so the match will undoubtedly go ahead.» The word so gives the reason, and undoubtedly shows the writer is confident. Ask yourself: is the writer sure, or only guessing? If they are sure, undoubtedly fits.
explain: Try swapping in certainly. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Writers use undoubtedly when they want the reader to believe them, so it is a word for a strong opinion.
fact: Undoubtedly is an adverb: it tells you how sure something is.
fact: «Undoubtedly» means certainly, without any doubt.
fact: A writer uses «undoubtedly» to show they are confident, or to show a known fact.
fact: In a story, a boastful character may say they are «undoubtedly» the best, and the reader may not believe them.
exercise: «Ella has undoubtedly finished her homework, because she was at the desk all evening.» What does undoubtedly mean here? | Maybe, but only a little | Not at all | Quickly and quietly | *Certainly, with no doubt
exercise: «The bridge is undoubtedly strong, so the trucks can cross it.» Find and copy the word that shows the writer is sure. | trucks | *undoubtedly | strong | the
exercise: Toad says he is undoubtedly the cleverest animal in the river. Why might the reader doubt him? | Undoubtedly means he is not sure at all | *Toad is boasting, so the reader may not believe him | Toad is always right about everything | Toad is a fish, so he cannot be clever
test: Which word means the same as undoubtedly? | Perhaps | Maybe | *Certainly | Sometimes
test: «The dog will undoubtedly be hungry after its long run.» What does undoubtedly tell you? | The writer is guessing | The writer is angry with the dog | *The writer is sure, with no doubt | The writer is asking a question
exam: Which sentence shows that something is certain? | *The sun will undoubtedly rise tomorrow. | Perhaps undoubtedly the cat is asleep. | The bus may undoubtedly be late, I think. | Undoubtedly, I might be wrong, but I hope not.
